Review follow-up for session workspace deletion.

Decision: deleting or archiving a Beaver conversation never removes its managed work directory, default outputs, or user-configured outputs. These files belong to the user and are cleaned up only through an explicit filesystem action outside this session lifecycle. The automatic workspace cleanup module was removed.

Deletion no longer deserializes the session first, so a corrupt conversation file can still be removed. Failure to remove the conversation file itself remains blocking; unrelated workspace file state cannot block conversation deletion.

Configured output roots are canonicalized before workspace-drift comparison, preventing false notices when the configured location is reached through a symbolic link or platform shortcut.

Tests cover corrupt-session deletion, preservation of work and default deliverables, and canonical output-root comparison. Validation: 2495 Rust tests passed; cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings, cargo fmt --check, git diff --check, and graphify update . passed.
